"id": "in-a-country-churchyard",
"text": "{title: In A Country Churchyard}\n[Intro:]\n| [G] [D] [C] | [G] |\n\n[G]In a country [D]churchyard there's a [C]preacher with his [G]people\n[C]gathered all [G]around to [Am7]join a man and [D]woman.\n[G]Spring is here and [D]turtle doves are [C]singing from the [G]steeple,\n[C]bees are in the flo[G]wers [Am7]growing in the [D]graveyard,\n[B]and over the [Em]hill, where [C]the river [D]meets the [G]mill,\na [C]lovely girl is [G]coming down to [Am]give her hand up [D]on her\n[G]wedding day.\n\nDressed in simple white and wearing flowers in her hair,\nmusic as she walks slowly to the altar.\nPicking up his bible then the preacher turns towards her.\n\"Will you take this man to be your wedded husband,\nto honor and love in the eyes of god above.\nNow let the people sing with me these words to live forever\nin your heart.\"\n\n[C]Let [D]your [Em]love [Bm]    [C]shine [G]on, [Em]for we are [Bm]the stars in [C]the sky.\n[C]Let [D]your [Em]love [Bm]    [C]shin[G]e strong [C]until the [D]day [C]you fly.  [G] [D] [C]\n\nMany years have fallen on that golden country morning,\ngraveyards overgrown, the church lies in ruins.\nIvy on the walls and ravens wheeling high above me\nas I make my way towards the last remaining headstone,\nI fell to my knees, read the lines beneath the leaves,\nand suddenly it seemed to me I heard the words like singing\nin the trees.\n\nLet your love... (repeat 1x)\n\n    ...[C]fly [G]away  [C] [G] [D] [C] [G] [D] [C] [G]"
